  "questionLabels": [],
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the given figure, the charge stored in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> capacitor, when points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> are joined by a connecting wire is _______<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/bca034fb-7bba-4a95-9797-f9200cca7cde.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 320px;\"/></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "36",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>At steady state, capacitor behaves as an open circuit and current flows in circuit as shown in the diagram.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/80cf28e5-7735-4298-8a5f-2a9848a2037b.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 368px;\"/></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>eq</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo> </mo><mi>Ω</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mi>Ω</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Δ</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>Ω</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p>So, potential difference across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo> </mo><mi>V</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>Δ</mi><mi>V</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn><mo> </mo><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
